# Git commits

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- Common types: **`feat`**, **`fix`**, **`docs`**, **`chore`**, **`ci`**, **`test`**, **`refactor`**, **`perf`**.
- **Scopes** examples: `core`, `wasm`, `web`, `spec`, `ci`.
- Breaking changes: **`!`** after the type/scope (`feat(wasm)!: ...`) and/or a **`BREAKING CHANGE:`** footer.

Keep the subject line **imperative** and **~72 characters or fewer**.
